1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:01,767
<i>This time,
I want to do it right, Andrew.</i>

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,467
<i>Just think of it like
you didn't fall for him.</i>

3
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:05,100
<i> That's easy, right?</i>

4
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:06,167
<i> Yvette, I know in my heart</i>

5
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,833
<i>that she could never do this
to herself.</i>

6
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:08,967
<i> So, who would do this?</i>

7
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,800
<i>We will never know
until she wakes up.</i>

8
00:00:10,933 --> 00:00:12,467
<i>Why doesn't his name show up
in our files?</i>

9
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:13,900
<i> His name is not real.</i>

10
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:14,733
<i> What's his name?</i>

11
00:00:14,867 --> 00:00:16,067
<i> Kang Dae-Hyun.</i>

12
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,567
<i> Joey, listen carefully.</i>

13
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,033
<i> Jin Ho is a criminal.</i>

14
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:20,800
<i> Don't go with him. Joey!</i>

15
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:22,833
<i>I know I have a lot
of explaining to do.</i>

16
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:24,067
<i> I have to go.</i>

17
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,667
<i> I think he knows Berdugo.</i>

18
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,567
<i> How can we find that out?</i>

19
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,600
<i> I thought of another way.</i>

20
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,867
[GRUNTS]

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,900
Are you really trying to test
my patience?

22
00:00:59,033 --> 00:01:02,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

23
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,600
Clearly, you're upset again.

24
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:07,400
What did I do this time?

25
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,533
Now, you're asking?

26
00:01:09,667 --> 00:01:12,267
Why didn't you tell me
that you're leaving?

27
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,700
I didn't know
that I'm a prisoner here.

28
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:17,000
You're not.

29
00:01:17,133 --> 00:01:19,967
You're acting like you're not
part of this operation.

30
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:21,467
Am I?

31
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:26,067
All I do is watch what is
happening in the factory.

32
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,500
That's an important task!

33
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:30,200
But you know I can do more
than babysit!

34
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:34,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

35
00:01:37,067 --> 00:01:38,467
Theresa.

36
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,267
If you give me a chance
to talk to Berdugo,

37
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:44,467
I can make you trust me
to do bigger responsibilities

38
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,333
with bigger rewards.

39
00:01:48,967 --> 00:01:51,900
He'll be here tomorrow
to check our operations,

40
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:55,233
so you better make sure
to make a good impression.

41
00:01:55,367 --> 00:01:57,333
My name is on the line here,

42
00:01:57,467 --> 00:01:59,467
so don't ruin your chance.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,067
I won't.

44
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,333
Oh, dear...

45
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,400
you haven't slept yet.

46
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:14,333
Why are you still awake?

47
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,067
Mom...

48
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:18,167
I really can't sleep,

49
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:20,933
so I'm just doing some thinking.

50
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:25,300
How about you?

51
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:28,467
Ma'am Yvette asked me to
accompany her to the hospital.

52
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:37,633
Mom, how's Ma'am Rebecca?

53
00:02:37,767 --> 00:02:39,533
She's out of the ICU.

54
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:41,567
She's in a private room now.

55
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,100
Her condition is improving,

56
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:47,433
but she's still unconscious.

57
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:51,567
Is Andrew there?

58
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:52,667
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,200
Yes, he's still watching over
his mother.

60
00:02:56,567 --> 00:02:59,267
How is he? Is he okay?

61
00:03:00,767 --> 00:03:04,867
You know, you're both asking
the same question.

62
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,133
He asked me how you were.

63
00:03:07,267 --> 00:03:08,767
I told him...

64
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,400
you're fine.

65
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:15,400
But is that true, child?

66
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:17,533
Are you really okay?

67
00:03:17,667 --> 00:03:19,733
Of course,
why wouldn't I be?

68
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:23,367
Because it's obvious
that you're concerned.

69
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:28,133
The truth is, dear,
it's clear that Boss Idol

70
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:31,400
is confused about what happened
to his mother.

71
00:03:31,533 --> 00:03:33,667
He can't understand

72
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,967
how Ma'am Rebecca ended up
like this.

73
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:42,900
Mom, about Ma'am Yvette's
husband...

75
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,500
The suspicion you had about him,

76
00:03:44,633 --> 00:03:46,300
did you tell her?

77
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:50,267
I don't know
if I should say something.

78
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,667
Child, Sir Tomas seems fine.

79
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,900
He's good to his family,

80
00:03:57,033 --> 00:03:59,267
especially to Andrew.

81
00:03:59,967 --> 00:04:03,133
It's hard to make accusations.

82
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:09,167
Maybe we're just giving
too much meaning

83
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,933
to what Ma'am Rebecca said.

84
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:21,067
I hope so, Mom.

85
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:22,567 --> 00:04:25,633
I hope Ma'am Rebecca
recovers soon.

87
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,333
So, Andrew won't worry anymore.

88
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,567
- That's right.
- So...

89
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:32,833
that we'll finally
know the truth

90
00:04:32,967 --> 00:04:35,133
about what really happened.

91
00:04:35,267 --> 00:04:39,700
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

92
00:04:42,433 --> 00:04:46,567
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

93
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:59,600
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:05:09,467 --> 00:05:13,500
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:26,833
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:41,000
Mom, I always want
to be like you.

97
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,733
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:05:42,867 --> 00:05:46,933
The person who can say
everything.

99
00:05:48,667 --> 00:05:50,133
But...

100
00:05:51,367 --> 00:05:54,033
I don't know why,
but when it comes to Joey,

101
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,767
I can't admit it.

102
00:05:59,767 --> 00:06:01,300
<i> Do you still love her?</i>

103
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:04,500
<i>Actually, I already love
someone else,</i>

104
00:06:04,633 --> 00:06:06,367
<i> family,</i>

105
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:09,233
<i> friends like you.</i>

106
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:11,100
<i> You love me already?</i>

107
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:16,233
Before, I wanted to ask you
about work...

108
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,200
but now it's personal.

109
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:25,200
Mom, please wake up.

110
00:06:26,367 --> 00:06:29,300
I really need your advice.

111
00:06:32,133 --> 00:06:36,100
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:06:39,467 --> 00:06:40,800
Mom?

113
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,333
Mom, can you hear me?

114
00:06:47,233 --> 00:06:50,567
Squeeze my hand if you do.

115
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:54,733
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,833
Sir, good morning! Welcome back!

117
00:07:02,967 --> 00:07:04,600
Your motorpart is good now.

118
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:06,067
Finally!

119
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,800
You took care of my baby, right?

120
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,233
Yes, Sir!

121
00:07:10,233 --> 00:07:11,900
Sir, have seat.

122
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:13,633
Thank you.

123
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:24,267
[♪INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING♪]

124
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,867
[PHONE RINGS]

125
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,267
Hello, Sir?

126
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,833
This is the shop.

127
00:07:36,967 --> 00:07:39,400
Are you sure that's the Korean
we're looking for?

128
00:07:39,533 --> 00:07:40,633
- Yes.
- Okay, thanks.

129
00:07:40,767 --> 00:07:41,767
I'm on my way.

130
00:07:42,967 --> 00:07:43,900
Dad...

131
00:07:44,033 --> 00:07:45,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:46,933
you're leaving?
You're going out?

133
00:07:47,067 --> 00:07:49,300
It's dangerous,
someone might see you.

134
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:50,767
I'll be careful.

135
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:53,200
And I'm prepared.

136
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:54,467
Dad, even so.

137
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,267
I'll come with you.

138
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,500
Dad, please.

139
00:07:57,633 --> 00:07:59,800
You're going
to see Jin Ho, right?

140
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:01,733
I'm coming with you.

141
00:08:01,867 --> 00:08:03,167
No, you shouldn't.

142
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:06,533
It's dangerous
and I'm just going to tail him.

143
00:08:06,667 --> 00:08:08,133
Oh, that's even better.

144
00:08:08,267 --> 00:08:10,100
You're just going to follow him.

145
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:12,700
Please say yes, Dad.

146
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,033
I promise, I will behave.

147
00:08:14,167 --> 00:08:15,933
I won't pester you.

148
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:17,267
I just want to see for myself

149
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,500
if what you said
about Jin Ho is true

150
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:22,633
that he's a criminal
and part of the syndicate.

151
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:28,800
What happened was reflexive
movement.

152
00:08:28,933 --> 00:08:31,367
These are automatic responses
to stimuli

153
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,867
such as finger twitching

154
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,167
and response to touch
and loud noises.

155
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,633
I held mom's hand.

156
00:08:38,767 --> 00:08:40,967
That explains it.

157
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,233
But don't worry.

158
00:08:42,367 --> 00:08:44,867
That's a good sign
because at least,

159
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,700
we know the patient's body
still reacts,

160
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,533
even involuntarily.

161
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:53,267
We'll just monitor her.

162
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:56,233
Thank you, Doc.

163
00:08:56,367 --> 00:08:57,933
I'll leave you for now.

164
00:08:58,067 --> 00:08:59,933
All right, thank you.

165
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:04,933
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,000
Mom...

167
00:09:15,267 --> 00:09:18,467
I still don't know
how this happened to you.

168
00:09:19,867 --> 00:09:21,800
But I promise you...

169
00:09:22,767 --> 00:09:24,833
I'll do everything.

170
00:09:24,967 --> 00:09:29,067
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

171
00:09:39,967 --> 00:09:42,500
Make sure everything
is in order, Lisa.

172
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:45,133
<i>You're still making up
for your past mistakes.</i>

173
00:09:45,267 --> 00:09:46,367
I know, Berdugo.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,933
I also want to meet the man
you brought into the group.

175
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:51,967
Yes, of course.

176
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,467
<i> Matias said</i>

177
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,833
he doesn't trust that man.

178
00:09:55,967 --> 00:09:59,167
Matias doesn't trust anyone.

179
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:02,300
You know, he's paranoid.

180
00:10:02,467 --> 00:10:04,367
<i> But believe me...</i>

181
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,000
You can trust my guy.

182
00:10:06,133 --> 00:10:08,100
I'll be the judge of that.

183
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:12,267
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:21,167
There he is.

185
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:24,333
Do you want me to go straight
to him, ask him?

186
00:10:24,467 --> 00:10:26,233
"Where's Berdugo?"

187
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:27,267
No!

188
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,400
You said you'd behave, remember?

189
00:10:29,533 --> 00:10:30,967
Stay here!

190
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:34,767
You're so tense, Dad.
I'm just joking, sorry.

191
00:10:34,933 --> 00:10:36,767
You and your jokes!

192
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:40,033
You know this is serious.

193
00:10:41,367 --> 00:10:43,300
I want my normal life back.

194
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:45,333
I don't want to keep hiding.

195
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:49,167
I also want Berdugo's
iniquity to end.

196
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:53,400
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,233
<i> You ready to go?</i>

198
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,600
Who is he talking to?

199
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,833
Let's follow him.

200
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:17,867
Never say die?

201
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,667
Never say die.

202
00:11:19,967 --> 00:11:23,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

203
00:11:25,833 --> 00:11:26,867
Dad, move closer.

204
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,500
They might get away.

205
00:11:29,633 --> 00:11:31,133
This is near enough.

206
00:11:31,267 --> 00:11:33,033
They might notice us.

207
00:11:33,167 --> 00:11:36,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:46,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

209
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,733
Dad, why did they stop?

210
00:12:01,467 --> 00:12:03,067
I don't know.

211
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:09,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,000
Where are we going?

213
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:12,900
Are we meeting Berdugo here?

214
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:15,433
No.

215
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,300
I'm just taking a breather.

216
00:12:18,367 --> 00:12:21,200
Are you worried about me
meeting him?

217
00:12:21,333 --> 00:12:24,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:12:24,167 --> 00:12:25,633
Don't be.

219
00:12:26,667 --> 00:12:28,600
You don't know him like I do.

220
00:12:28,733 --> 00:12:31,000
Even after all these years
in this job,

221
00:12:31,133 --> 00:12:33,133
I still get intimidated by him.

222
00:12:34,167 --> 00:12:35,933
If you are this scared,

223
00:12:36,067 --> 00:12:38,100
why don't you take
my suggestion?

224
00:12:38,233 --> 00:12:41,133
We can be our own boss
back in Korea.

225
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:44,600
We both know the ins and outs
of this business.

226
00:12:44,733 --> 00:12:46,900
I like what I do.

227
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:48,533
And besides,

228
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,667
you can't just get out
of Berdugo's organization.

229
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:54,600
Once you're in,
you can never leave.

230
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:57,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:11,933
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

232
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:16,400
Joey, hide!

233
00:13:16,533 --> 00:13:20,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

234
00:13:42,467 --> 00:13:45,133
[♪SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING♪]

235
00:13:45,267 --> 00:13:46,600
[CAT SNARLS]

236
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:51,100
Dad, that's Theresa!

237
00:13:51,233 --> 00:13:53,833
She's the woman Jin Ho
wants to capture.

238
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:55,333
And she's the woman
I told you about

239
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,367
who was there when Ramon
was killed!

240
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:00,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:14:00,767 --> 00:14:02,500
Are you sure that's the woman
in your video?

242
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,533
Yes, Dad, that's her!

243
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:09,900
[REVVING]

244
00:14:10,033 --> 00:14:13,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:14:23,533 --> 00:14:28,533
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:31,500
That's weird.

247
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:33,767
What?

248
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:37,067
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:14:38,667 --> 00:14:39,733
Don't mind them.

250
00:14:39,867 --> 00:14:41,400
Let's just go back.

251
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:43,567
Berdugo might be there already.

252
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:47,333
No, I really think
we're being followed.

253
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,767
Are you sure?

254
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:53,600
That car was parked behind us.

255
00:14:53,933 --> 00:14:55,100
I think something's wrong.

256
00:14:55,233 --> 00:14:56,933
I have a bad feeling about this.

257
00:14:57,067 --> 00:15:01,200
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:20,033
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [AMBULANCE SIREN WAILING]

259
00:15:21,933 --> 00:15:23,767
Dad, why did you stop?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,767
They'll escape!

261
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,967
Looks like they realized
we were following them.

262
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,567
Forget it.

263
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,033
We'll just get into trouble.

264
00:15:32,167 --> 00:15:34,867
But, Dad, this is our chance!

265
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:36,500
My child...

266
00:15:38,267 --> 00:15:40,533
Your safety is more important
to me.

267
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,267
Let them go.

268
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,400
We might just get into trouble.

269
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:50,867
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,300
Are you sure you didn't
notice anything

271
00:16:03,433 --> 00:16:06,767
the day something happened
to mommy?

272
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:09,300
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]
Maybe she ate something?

273
00:16:09,467 --> 00:16:10,500
No, nothing.

274
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:12,967
We ate the same food.

275
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,000
Who were here that day?

276
00:16:15,133 --> 00:16:19,367
Me, Ma'am Clarissa, the kids,

277
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:22,033
Ma'am Yvette, and Sir Tomas.

278
00:16:22,167 --> 00:16:23,533
Okay, thank you.

279
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,600
He's unbelievable, Dad.

280
00:16:32,733 --> 00:16:34,400
We treated him as a friend

281
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:36,667
but in return,
he did that to us?

282
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,933
Why would he do that, Dad?

283
00:16:39,067 --> 00:16:41,000
Because he was looking
for Theresa.

284
00:16:41,133 --> 00:16:44,267
Now, you became the key
when he saw your video.

285
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:46,933
If they really know each other,

286
00:16:47,067 --> 00:16:49,100
then they're together
in the syndicate.

287
00:16:50,367 --> 00:16:52,300
Does that mean...

288
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:53,600
Jin Ho might have told Theresa

289
00:16:53,733 --> 00:16:55,633
that I was the one
who took the video?

290
00:16:58,167 --> 00:17:00,833
But why wouldn't he reveal
my location?

291
00:17:02,567 --> 00:17:04,633
Maybe...

292
00:17:04,767 --> 00:17:08,700
Maybe he used our friendship
to get close to Theresa,

293
00:17:08,833 --> 00:17:11,333
not to hurt me, Dad.

294
00:17:12,567 --> 00:17:14,267
We don't know for sure.

295
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:17,633
We don't know
what their plan is.

296
00:17:18,767 --> 00:17:21,400
But what's important is
to catch them

297
00:17:21,533 --> 00:17:23,600
so nothing happens to you.

298
00:17:23,733 --> 00:17:25,867
"Nothing happens"?

299
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,400
Miguel, you keep going out.

300
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:32,100
Someone might see you.

301
00:17:32,233 --> 00:17:34,967
Are you two planning
something again?

302
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:37,400
You're just...

303
00:17:37,533 --> 00:17:39,800
too suspicious.

304
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,567
Let's just go upstairs.

305
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:44,133
- Okay? Let's go upstairs.
- You're planning something...

306
00:17:44,267 --> 00:17:47,167
No, you're just too suspicious.

307
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,900
Joey?

308
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,400
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

309
00:17:53,367 --> 00:17:55,067
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

310
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,300
Kisses?

311
00:17:57,433 --> 00:17:58,967
Uncle Andrew...

312
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:03,200
How are you?

313
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:04,767
I know you miss
your grandmother...

314
00:18:06,233 --> 00:18:07,533
because I do too.

315
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:10,567
Will it take long
before she comes home?

316
00:18:15,833 --> 00:18:17,267
I don't know.

317
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:22,000
But I'm sure
she'll get better,

318
00:18:22,167 --> 00:18:25,967
because many people are waiting
for her, like you.

319
00:18:27,167 --> 00:18:31,700
She misses grandmother too,
Uncle.

320
00:18:31,833 --> 00:18:33,167
<i> Of course.</i>

321
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:37,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,867
Anyways, I have to go.

323
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:46,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:04,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

325
00:19:04,267 --> 00:19:06,933
Why aren't the shipments
for tomorrow packed yet?

326
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:08,967
Shouldn't they be ready?

327
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,000
Idiots!

328
00:19:10,133 --> 00:19:12,433
Don't scold them.

329
00:19:13,633 --> 00:19:16,767
I told them that I will check
the goods first.

330
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:18,067
Relax.

331
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,233
I'll do that later.

332
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:22,800
Go ahead, go back there now.

333
00:19:22,933 --> 00:19:27,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

334
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:29,433
What if Berdugo asks?

335
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:33,900
You know this isn't how
our operation works, right?

336
00:19:34,033 --> 00:19:35,600
Where did you come from?

337
00:19:35,733 --> 00:19:37,733
Looks like you were just busy
flirting.

338
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:40,100
Don't talk to me like that.

339
00:19:41,333 --> 00:19:42,733
So what?

340
00:19:42,867 --> 00:19:45,500
I don't care what you do.

341
00:19:45,633 --> 00:19:49,000
What matters to me
is this operation!

342
00:19:50,667 --> 00:19:52,233
Don't do that again.

343
00:19:55,333 --> 00:19:56,900
Are you going to fight me?

344
00:19:57,833 --> 00:19:59,400
Stop speaking in English.

345
00:19:59,533 --> 00:20:01,433
What are you talking about?

346
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,900
You've got nothing to brag
about.

347
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:06,300
Tell your dog to behave.

348
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:07,900
Or he's gonna get it from me.

349
00:20:08,033 --> 00:20:12,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,633
<i> What's this?</i>

351
00:20:22,533 --> 00:20:24,167
Oh, no!

352
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:27,400
Kisses...

353
00:20:27,867 --> 00:20:29,167
<i> What happened?</i>

354
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:30,667
I broke it, Harris.

355
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,267
I'm sorry.

356
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,733
Don't cry.

357
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,067
We can fix it.

358
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,133
We'll just ask mommy to fix it,
okay?

359
00:20:38,267 --> 00:20:39,700
Let me see.

360
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:44,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

361
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:46,633
Wait, what's this?

362
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
What's this?

363
00:20:53,133 --> 00:20:55,467
I found this inside.

364
00:20:56,767 --> 00:20:59,600
Looks like a camera.

365
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,033
[THUDS]

366
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:04,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

367
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,333
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

368
00:21:07,033 --> 00:21:10,500
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

369
00:21:12,033 --> 00:21:14,133
[THUDS AND CLACKS]

370
00:21:14,267 --> 00:21:16,100
Stop this nonsense!

371
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:19,267
Is this how you really are
when I'm not here?

372
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:21,000
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

373
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:24,067
Is this how you handle
this place?

374
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,467
It's not our fault.

375
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:26,700
I'm not talking to you.

376
00:21:26,833 --> 00:21:28,967
Sorry about that, Berdugo.

377
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,133
They just hate each other.

378
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:34,067
I promise this is the first
and the last time

379
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,167
that this will happen.

380
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,767
I hope so.

381
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:40,400
Because if not,
I'll fix it myself.

382
00:21:40,533 --> 00:21:42,100
And I promise you...

383
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:44,167
you won't like it.

384
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:46,433
I don't want to waste my time.

385
00:21:46,567 --> 00:21:48,233
Let's start the meeting.

386
00:21:48,367 --> 00:21:52,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:21:54,667 --> 00:21:56,567
We're not done yet.

388
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:00,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

389
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,333
- My child...
- Mom...

390
00:22:16,433 --> 00:22:17,767
Are you okay?

391
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:20,167
You've been pacing around.

392
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:26,700
No, I'm just trying to reach
10,000 steps to stay sexy.

393
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:31,233
Oh, my daughter's
really grown up.

394
00:22:31,367 --> 00:22:33,700
You're conscious
of your body now.

395
00:22:33,833 --> 00:22:36,033
Who are you trying
to look good for?

396
00:22:36,167 --> 00:22:38,500
- Andrew?
- Andrew? No!

397
00:22:38,633 --> 00:22:41,767
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]
He's just my friend.

398
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:44,767
Dear, you're being way
too defensive.

399
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:47,667
You know, I have no problems
with that.

400
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:51,500
Just don't forget
your priorities,

401
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:53,600
especially your studies.

402
00:22:54,567 --> 00:22:56,500
Speaking of Andrew,

403
00:22:56,633 --> 00:22:58,533
have you talked
to your boyfriend...

404
00:22:58,667 --> 00:23:01,767
I mean, your friend yet?

405
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:03,800
Not yet. Why?

406
00:23:03,933 --> 00:23:07,367
Andrew is going through
something heavy right now.

407
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:09,800
Aren't you concerned?

408
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:15,433
Call him.

409
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:25,367
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

410
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,633
Ma'am Zoey!

411
00:23:31,767 --> 00:23:32,833
Hi!

412
00:23:32,967 --> 00:23:34,367
Where's Andrew?

413
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,800
He went to his room.

414
00:23:36,933 --> 00:23:38,433
- Ah, okay.
- All right, Ma'am.

415
00:23:38,567 --> 00:23:40,667
Okay, thanks.

416
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:47,367
[PHONE RINGING]

417
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:51,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:23:53,267 --> 00:23:56,100
[PHONE RINGING]

419
00:23:56,767 --> 00:24:00,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

420
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:07,000
Joey!

421
00:24:07,133 --> 00:24:08,767
<i> Hi!</i>

422
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:10,867
Why are you calling Andrew?

423
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,467
Zoey?

424
00:24:13,533 --> 00:24:14,867
Where's Andrew?

425
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,267
He's busy.

426
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:18,267
He's preparing things to bring
to the hospital

427
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,233
<i> for Mommy Rebecca.</i>

428
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:22,667
"Mommy Rebecca?"

429
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:24,233
Ah, yes.

430
00:24:24,367 --> 00:24:26,300
That's what I used to call her

431
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:28,833
when Andrew and I were together.

432
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,367
I guess I should get used

433
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:31,533
to calling her that again,

434
00:24:31,667 --> 00:24:34,567
especially now that Andrew
and I are doing okay.

435
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:38,167
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

436
00:24:39,267 --> 00:24:43,800
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

437
00:24:45,733 --> 00:24:47,333
Is someone looking for my
corpse?

438
00:24:47,467 --> 00:24:49,333
Maybe Berdugo thinks
differently.

439
00:24:49,467 --> 00:24:51,600
Then let's bury Miguel.

440
00:24:51,733 --> 00:24:53,600
- What happened to you?
- I wanted to see you.

441
00:24:53,733 --> 00:24:55,767
Enjoy your coffee
because it's your last.

442
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,300
You're doomed.

443
00:24:57,433 --> 00:24:58,867
Don't leave yet.

444
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,400
I'm curious
if this thing really works.

445
00:25:01,533 --> 00:25:03,133
You are Kang Dae-Hyun, correct?

446
00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:04,233
I have a problem.

447
00:25:04,367 --> 00:25:06,967
The cops already know
who I really am.

448
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:08,767
Good thing no one saw me.

449
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:09,967
I feel I'm being haunted.

450
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:11,567
I think I saw Delgado.

451
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:12,800
What?
